# Product version

The product version is `KERNEL_VERSION_MAJOR`, `KERNEL_VERSION_MINOR`, and `KERNEL_VERSION_PATCH_LEVEL` in `sdk/include/reactos/version.cmake`. This trunk keeps `KERNEL_VERSION_BUILD_TYPE` as `dev`. The runtime report in `sdk/include/reactos/runtimever.h` stays 10.0.19045. Do not copy it into the product version. Leave the DLL offset at major plus 42.

A ReactOS pull appends one entry to `REACTOS_LINEAGE_IMPORTS` in that file, in the same commit. The entry is that ReactOS version and its full commit, oldest first. A pull does not move `KERNEL_VERSION_MAJOR`, `KERNEL_VERSION_MINOR`, or `KERNEL_VERSION_PATCH_LEVEL`.

Bump in the same commit that newly meets a gate below. The subject starts with `[VER]` and names the new version. Add the code's module tag after it. The body names the gate, then why the code changed.

```text
[VER] [SETUPLIB] Open 0.1.1-dev

0.1.0's release gate is the in-place upgrade. The kept disk
takes this build without a format, and 7-Zip still opens.
```

If a gate is already met on trunk and the version was not moved, move it before other work. That commit's subject is the version change. Leave boot-log fixtures and older dashboard snapshots on the version they recorded.

Milestones 34 through 40 do not move this number. A dashboard score, one matching syscall, or the runtime report does not either.

## Patch

Each gate below moves the patch once, from `0.1.N-dev` to `0.1.(N+1)-dev`, the first time it becomes true. One commit that newly meets two gates moves the patch by two.

- Milestone 13 is closed. The kept disk upgrades in place, the desktop appears, and 7-Zip still opens. `0.1.0-dev` becomes `0.1.1-dev`.
- Milestones 18 and 19 are both closed.
- Milestone 28 is closed.
- Milestone 31 is closed.
- Milestone 33 is closed and the minor gate below is not met. Do not open another 0.1 patch after the minor moves.

## Minor

Set `0.2.0-dev` in the commit where every line below is true. The patch resets to 0. Do not also add a 0.1 patch in that commit.

- Milestone 33 is closed. The root build is `_WIN32_WINNT=0x0A00` and `NTDDI_VERSION=0x0A00000B`.
- Milestone 13 upgrades the last 0.1 install without formatting, the desktop appears, and 7-Zip still opens.
- Milestone 15 service numbers are in the tree, and milestone 33 has frozen `sysfuncs64.h`.
- Page-table write and dirty bits stay where milestone 32 left them.
- `KmWin2k3VersionLie` still reports 5.2.3790. In-tree PE stamps stay 5.2.

## Major

Set `1.0.0-dev` only after a 0.2 version is already on trunk. Do not jump from 0.1.

- Milestones 24, 28, and 31 are closed.
- Milestone 13 upgrades a 0.2 install without formatting, and the catalog programs still complete their one action.
- `sysfuncs64.h` and the shared layouts from milestone 22 stay frozen on the 1.0 line.

A later 1.x patch or minor is a release cut on purpose. The next major is the commit that forces a format, or that breaks those frozen service numbers or shared layouts. DLL file versions follow the existing plus-42 rule, so 1.0.0 publishes 43.0.0.
